From: Carlos Cabrera H. <6750732+ccabrerah@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 24] ggml-sycl: 2-4-column Q5_K / Q6_K matvecs through the reordered ESIMD kernels

GGML_SYCL_DMMV_NCOLS=1. A 2..4-column MUL_MAT of a reordered Q5_K or Q6_K weight (the MTP verify step's positions) left
the one-column ESIMD kernel for the generic reordered MMVQ (q8_1 activations), ~1.4x a one-column call at two columns.
Here the row pair's blocks are dequantized once into 256 floats each -- the same values in the same chunk order as the
one-column kernel's mac_pair -- and MACed against every column's f32 activation, so each column is accumulated as the
one-column kernel accumulates it. Routed only on the reordered ESIMD path, single-device buffers, contiguous src1/dst.

